      "writtenOn": "2025-05-02T23:13:23Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why do we need a separate denylist for SCO and call since we\u0027re just checking both in the same conditional?",
      "revId": "a9c80f3e4b58240f33b25efaba67afb4ff0d9050",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0f54b7bd_932d9a93",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 13
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 1902235
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-05-04T17:50:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There are cases where SCO/eSCO is not connected when call is present but the headset or car kit does not want the link to be in sniff mode. So, we need two separate denylists.",
      "parentUuid": "11b820bc_ffdf6aea",
      "revId": "a9c80f3e4b58240f33b25efaba67afb4ff0d9050",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6532a2e2_3ead43b0",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 13
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 3469321
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-05-27T23:01:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Satish, could you please describe the scenario. Call is not over SCO and carkit still doesnt want link to go to sniff ?\n\nare we saying Carkit is trying to hold the link Active for indicators?",
      "parentUuid": "0f54b7bd_932d9a93",
      "revId": "a9c80f3e4b58240f33b25efaba67afb4ff0d9050",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "890e85d0_54bf299d",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 13
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 3865300
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-05-30T05:34:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If SCO gets disconnected during call, sniff gets enabled and may create issue with next SCO connection.\nWe are checking for call\u0027s presence before changing sniff policy if the device is deny-listed for disabling sniff during SCO and during call.",
      "parentUuid": "6532a2e2_3ead43b0",
      "revId": "a9c80f3e4b58240f33b25efaba67afb4ff0d9050",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "51b6e854_20eeb9cf",
        "filename": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
        "patchSetId": 13
      },
      "lineNbr": 0,
      "author": {
        "id": 3865300
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-05-30T05:34:56Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We need to keep link active if SCO gets disconnected during the call. If sniff is enabled, it may create issue with next SCO connection.\n\nSo, we are checking for call presence before changing sniff policy if the device is denylisted for disabling sniff during both SCO and call.",
      "parentUuid": "6532a2e2_3ead43b0",
      "revId": "a9c80f3e4b58240f33b25efaba67afb4ff0d9050",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
